column3:
Builds the general.dat summary: the active nations (two groups), the human managers with club and nation, the game date, the version, the play time and time(). `build_save_game_summary(summary)` (cdecl): the summary that `save_game_data` writes into `general.dat` (right after the version): 
 - +0: the nations of the league table (`G_LEAGUE_TABLE`, 0x23 of 0x48 bytes) with bit 2 set in `league_selected()`, the first through sprintf with its own name as the format (`FN_CRT_SPRINTF`), the others through the translated ", <%s>" (`FN_LANGLIB_SPRINTF`); +1000 (0x3e8): the same with bit 1; 
 - 16 managers, from the last of the person table (`G_STAFF_TABLE`, `staff::SIZE` bytes) backwards: a human one (`classification()` = 1) gives the name at +0x7e4 + 0x78 × i (`database_format_staff_name`, 200) and at +0x820 + 0x78 × i "club / nation" (`club_job()` and `national_job()`, name at `club::SHORT_NAME` / `nation::SHORT_NAME` of each), only one of them, or nothing; a non-human one only zeroes the name (the club stays as it was in the caller's buffer); 
 - `save_summary::GAME_DATE` the game date (`exe::date_operator_3d` of `G_CURRENT_DATE`), +0x7d0 the version (`exe::utils_get_version_string`), +0xf6c the play time (`G_GAME_PLAY_TIME_TOTAL` += time() − `G_GAME_PLAY_TIME_LAST_STAMP`; `G_GAME_PLAY_TIME_LAST_STAMP` = time()) and +0xf70 the time().
